//! Translation of `Tests/CoveUIRuntimeTests/ProgressiveImageTests.swift`.
//!
//! An incomplete progressive JPEG must still produce a real, aspect-preserving
//! preview, orientation must follow EXIF, and the allocation limits must hold
//! before anything is decoded.
//!
//! Fixtures: the Swift suite synthesised its JPEG through ImageIO at test time.
//! This crate has no encoder, so the same 256x128 yellow/green-noise image was
//! encoded once with `cjpeg -progressive -quality 85` and committed here as
//! literal bytes, plus a copy with a minimal EXIF APP1 carrying Orientation 6.
//! Both are real progressive JPEGs (10 SOS markers), so the partial-prefix case
//! exercises the actual incremental decoder rather than a stub.
//!
//! Behaviour checklist:
//! - an incomplete progressive JPEG produces an aspect-preserving preview with real pixels
//! - preview geometry follows EXIF orientation and never upscales
//! - preview allocation obeys source pixels
//! - preview allocation obeys bounded target dimensions
//! - empty and truncated data produce no preview

use cove_imaging::{ImageDecoder, PixelSize};

